# Here i used simple KQL to see who was the CEO using simple KQL

Kusto Query Language (KQL) - Kusto Query Language (KQL) is a powerful tool for exploring my data and discovering patterns, identifying anomalies and outliers. This language is used by Cyber Security Analysts Backend Developers.

### here is a baisc KQL script

Employees 

| where role == "CEO"


-As you can see 'Employees' I can use this to get the data of Employees for the company

- Then use | to find the source of data

- The pipeline character *'|'*, 

- After that I then add *'where'* operator 

-Now I use a column aka the *'role'* 

- Then now use comparison operator like equality operator and value *'=="CEO"* ' 

-I get to employee needed which is the CEO and their data i.e. their email address

- Important note KQL is case sensitive



